00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.680
Just as a refresher,

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:16.940
if A is a matrix whose shape is
n by d,

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:21.260
remember that means n rows and d
columns,

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:25.960
what must the shape of x be for
it to be legal to multiply A by

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:26.960
x?

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:37.740
Yeah, x has to have d rows in
it, because the golden rule of

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:42.020
matrix multiplication told us
the number of columns in the

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:44.940
first object must equal the
number of rows in the second

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:45.940
object.

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:50.360
And here, if x is a vector, that
means it has one column.

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:54.860
But this means I could have
multiplied A on the right

00:05:54.880 --> 00:06:00.130
by any matrix that had d rows
and any number of columns.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:04.740
I just happened to choose a
vector.

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:06.740
And so the result,

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:07.740
Ax,

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:13.680
what type of object is it?

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:19.580
What type of object is it?

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:22.200
Ax, is it a number? Is it a
matrix?

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:24.980
Is it a vector? There's
something else.

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:27.760
Yeah? In the n by 1 matrix.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:29.500
Yeah, which I would call a
vector.

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:30.500
Yeah.

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:33.740
Technically, it's a matrix as
well.

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:39.740
I'll say this is a vector in Rn.

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:45.400
And just so it seems symmetric
here, I'll call this a vector in

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:46.580
Rd.

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:50.760
And its shape is n by 1.

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:53.540
Where did the shape come from?

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:58.040
Well, what we saw is that when
you are multiplying two objects,

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:01.790
the inner dimensions must match.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:04.900
Those are the highlighted d's.

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:07.400
And then the outer dimensions
tell you the shape of the

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:08.020
result.

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:11.420
So this is saying the fact that
I've highlighted the two d's

00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:15.040
tells me, OK, it is legal to
multiply a by x,

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:19.140
and the output is going to be n
by 1, which is a vector in Rn.

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:20.640
OK, good.

00:07:20.780 --> 00:07:26.540
So that means this is a legal
operation here, because Ax is a

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:30.620
vector in Rn, and we can find
the length of a vector.

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:36.400
Whereas if instead I asked you
